; SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
; (MPL-2.0 preferred; MPL-2.0 required for npm ecosystem compatibility)
; INTENT.contractile — Purpose and scope for polyglot-i18n
; Helps LLM/SLM agents understand what this repo IS and IS NOT.
;
; Part of the contractile family: MUST, TRUST, DUST, INTENT, ADJUST

; ── Definitions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; INTENT (noun)
;   The purpose contractile. Defines what this repository IS, what it is
;   NOT (anti-purpose), and which architectural decisions are load-bearing.
;   Without INTENT, LLMs drift into scope creep, reverse key decisions,
;   or add features that belong in a different repo.
;
; Scope:
;   INTENT governs the conceptual boundaries of the project — its reason
;   for existing, its domain, and its relationship to the ecosystem.
;   It does NOT specify implementation details (that's MUST and code).
;
; Relationship to other contractiles:
;   - MUST: INTENT explains WHY certain MUSTs exist. If you don't
;     understand a MUST, read INTENT first.
;   - TRUST: The "ask-before-touching" section in INTENT maps directly
;     to TRUST.trust-deny for the most sensitive areas.
;   - ADJUST: INTENT's anti-purpose should include "this software is
;     NOT only for users with perfect vision/hearing/mobility."
;   - DUST: When INTENT changes (repo pivots), related DUST entries
;     should be created for the abandoned direction.
;
; ── End Definitions ──────────────────────────────────────────────

(intent-contractile
  (version "1.0.0")
  (repo "polyglot-i18n")

  ; === Purpose (what this repo IS) ===
  (purpose
    "polyglot-i18n is a ReScript-first internationalization library for
     JavaScript runtimes (Deno, Node.js). It is a modernised fork of i18n-node
     by Marcus Spiegel, providing translation functions (__(), __n(), __mf()),
     CLDR plural rules, locale detection, and MessageFormat support. The library
     is being migrated from JavaScript to ReScript with optional WASM
     acceleration for hot paths. It includes NLP features (stemming, fuzzy
     matching, segmentation) and integrates with Express, Fastify, Hono, Koa,
     and NestJS as middleware."
  )

  ; === Anti-Purpose (what this repo is NOT — prevents scope creep) ===
  (anti-purpose
    "This is NOT a translation management system (TMS) — it does not provide
     a UI for translators. It is NOT a machine translation service — it reads
     pre-written translations from JSON files. It is NOT a CMS or content
     system — it only handles string translation. It is NOT a standalone
     application — it is a library consumed by other projects. It is NOT only
     for English-speaking developers — the API and docs must be clear for
     non-native English speakers (see ADJUST.contractile)."
  )

  ; === Key Architectural Decisions That Must Not Be Reversed ===
  (architectural-invariants
    ("ReScript as target language — all new features in ReScript, not JS/TS")
    ("WASM optional — always provide JS fallback, WASM is acceleration only")
    ("i18n-node API compatibility — __(), __n(), __mf() signatures preserved")
    ("JSON locale files — simple, editable, no binary formats for translations")
    ("Instance pattern over singleton — concurrent-safe by default")
    ("CLDR plural rules — follow the Unicode spec, no custom rule inventions")
    ("Middleware pattern — integrate via init(), do not require framework coupling")
  )

  ; === Sensitive Areas (if in doubt, ask) ===
  (ask-before-touching
    "src/core/Plural.res — CLDR rules, changes affect all language correctness"
    "src/core/I18n.res — public API surface, changes affect all consumers"
    "package.json — npm metadata, version, dependencies visible to consumers"
    "wasm/src/ — Rust WASM module, must match JS API exactly"
    "locales/ — default translation files, used as examples and in tests"
    ".machine_readable/ — checkpoint files, format is specified"
    "test/ — test suite, weakening tests is a MUST violation"
  )

  ; === Ecosystem Position ===
  (ecosystem
    (belongs-to "standalone")
    (depends-on ("@messageformat/core" "make-plural" "mustache" "fast-printf" "debug"))
    (depended-on-by ("any-js-app-needing-i18n"))
  )
)
